{title: We seemed like grasshoppers}
{subtitle: Numbers 13:22–33; 14:1–4; Deuteronomy 1:36; Joshua 14:12–15; 15:13–14; Judges 1:10–20}
{key: Dm}
{tempo: 85}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Dm] | [Dm] | [Dm] | [Dm] |
| [Dm] | [Dm] | [Dm] | [Bbmaj7] |
| [C] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Dm]They went up through the Negev and came to Hebron
[Bb]Where Ahiman and Sheshai [C]lived with Talmai
[Dm]Descendants of Anak in the ancient land
The [Bb]cities were fortified and [C]very large
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Pre-Chorus}
[Dm]In the Valley of Eshcol they cut a branch
[Bb]A single cluster of grapes on a pole [C]between them
[Dm]Forty days they spent in the scouting
[Bb]Then they returned to the Wilderness [C]of Paran
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Bb]We even saw the descen[Dm]dants of Anak there
[Bb]In our own eyes we seemed like [Dm]grasshoppers
[Bb]The land we traveled through de[Dm]vours the living
And all the [Bb]people we saw are of e[C]normous size
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Dm]The whole congregation broke out in a loud cry
[Bb]The people wept through that dark [C]and fearful night
[Dm]They grumbled against Moses and Aaron
[Bb]Saying if only we had [C]died in Egypt
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Pre-Chorus}
[Dm]Why is the LORD bringing us to this land
[Bb]Only to fall by the sword [C]and be plundered
[Dm]Our wives and children would become the spoils
[Bb]So let us choose a leader and [C]go back
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Bb]We even saw the descen[Dm]dants of Anak [Bb]there
In our own eyes we seemed [Dm]like grasshop[Bb]pers
The land we traveled through de[Dm]vours the living
And all the [Bb]people we saw are of e[C]normous size
{end_of_chorus}

{comment: Interlude}
| [Dm] | [Dm] | [Bb] | [C] |

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Dm]But Caleb quieted the people before Moses
[Bb]Saying we should go up and [C]take possession
[Dm]For we are well able to do it
Though the [Bb]men with him said we [C]cannot attack them
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Bb]We even saw the descen[Dm]dants of Anak [Bb]there
In our own eyes we [Dm]seemed like gras[Bb]shoppers
The land we traveled through [Dm]devours the living
And all [Bb]the people we saw are of [C]enormous [Dm]size
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
Caleb drove out Sheshai, Ahiman, and Talmai
[Bb]Hebron belonged to him as [C]an inheri[Bb]tance
Because he followed the [C]LORD wholehearted[Dm]ly
{end_of_verse}

{comment: Outro (instrumental)}
